# MSX development (always)

## Product (locked)

- Name: **MSXTT** (combined MSX1 Screen 2 / MSX2 Screen 5 Teletekst)
- Slim COM: **MSXTT.COM**. AUTOEXEC runs UNAPI then MSXTT.COM.
- Detect MSX1 via `Sys_GetMSXVersion() == 0`; anything else is Screen 5.
- Format: **DOS2** `.COM`. ROM later (`ROM_16K_P2` at 8000h) when asked.
- Framework path: `MSXgl/` in this repo
- Teletekst charset: hybrid 6×8 (`src/tt/tt_font.h`).

## Stack

- Language: C, with selective Z80 assembly
- Framework: MSXgl · Compiler: SDCC (bundled with MSXgl)
- Public build entry: `build.bat` / `Makefile`
- UNAPI client: `MSXgl/engine/src/network/unapi_tcp.*`
- Emulator: `tools/openmsxnet/openmsx.exe`

## Versioning

- Version lives only in `src/version.h` (`APP_VERSION`).
- Bump the last number by one for every change (`0.9.200` → `0.9.201`).
- Tag each commit `v<version>`. Author: rubikonlab@proton.me (do not change git config).

## Working principles

- After every UNAPI call, re-enable interrupts (`EnableInterrupt()`).
- Do not call `tcpip_tcp_flush`.
- Keypad rows 9–10: if `g_NEWKEY[9]` and `[10]` are all-pressed (`0x00`), there is no keypad.

## Debug ROM builds (hardware testers)

- Every new debug/hardened ROM bake must get a **unique filename** under `build/` and `emul/rom/` (and leave prior builds intact).
- Pattern: `MSXTT3.ROM`, `MSXTT3B.ROM`, `MSXTT3C.ROM`, … then `MSXTT4.ROM` / `MSXTT4B.ROM`, etc. Never overwrite a lettered debug ROM the tester may still be flashing.
- Also keep/update the “current” build output from the bat (e.g. `MSXTT3.ROM`) if the build script writes one, but always **copy** to the next unique letter name when shipping a new debug image.
